    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ae2da629a6fc0adadb153c1a346438b30b10ce6a4fa79c8dd539da77ee5fe52d",
      "text": "Day 4 · Breakfast at the hotel. Morning city tour (half day) of Buenos Aires’ many faces: the Obelisk, symbol of the city; Plaza de Mayo, Plaza San Martín and the Alvear area; Avenida Corrientes, Avenida de Mayo and Avenida 9 de Julio; historic La Boca and San Telmo, elegant Palermo and Recoleta, modern Puerto Madero; the Lezama and Tres de Febrero parks, the commercial and financial districts, a football stadium and much more. Free afternoon.\n\nEvening · Dinner and tango show at La Ventana, a renowned tango house in the heart of San Telmo that opened its doors in 1982. This fully restored historic conventillo offers a journey through Buenos Aires culture, with 32 artists on stage: two tango orchestras, a folk music group, dancers and singers. The menu combines international and typical Argentine dishes from the traditional charcoal grill, with a large Argentine wine cellar. Return to the hotel.",
